From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOYOUNG SEO <hy50.seo@samsung.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:18:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 026/117] scsi: ufs: core: Add a helper for the system suspend
 callbacks

Move the body of ufshcd_wl_suspend() into ufshcd_wl_system_suspend(), which
takes the PM operation as a parameter, so that it can be shared with
ufshcd_wl_poweroff() in the next patch. ufshcd_wl_suspend() calls it with
UFS_SYSTEM_PM.

No functional change, except that the error message printed when the
suspend fails now contains the name of the new function.

Suggested-by: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Signed-off-by: HOYOUNG SEO <hy50.seo@samsung.com>
Reviewed-by: Peter Wang <peter.wang@mediatek.com>
Reviewed-by: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/331418503.141794387787744.JavaMail.epsvc@epcpadp2new
Signed-off-by: Martin K. Petersen (Oracle) <mkp@kernel.org>

[mzak: picked for q91o (21 Nov gains plan) from linux-next/maintainer tree commit 280c35ec0099; mark V]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index 1ca89c67354b8..36a35072c7714 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -10756,7 +10756,7 @@ static int ufshcd_wl_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 #endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
-static int ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct device *dev)
+static int ufshcd_wl_system_suspend(struct device *dev, enum ufs_pm_op pm_op)
 {
 	struct scsi_device *sdev = to_scsi_device(dev);
 	struct ufs_hba *hba;
@@ -10769,7 +10769,7 @@ static int ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (pm_runtime_suspended(dev))
 		goto out;
 
-	ret = __ufshcd_wl_suspend(hba, UFS_SYSTEM_PM);
+	ret = __ufshcd_wl_suspend(hba, pm_op);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(&sdev->sdev_gendev, "%s failed: %d\n", __func__,  ret);
 		up(&hba->host_sem);
@@ -10785,6 +10785,11 @@ static int ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+static int ufshcd_wl_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return ufshcd_wl_system_suspend(dev, UFS_SYSTEM_PM);
+}
+
 static int ufshcd_wl_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct scsi_device *sdev = to_scsi_device(dev);
-- 
